  "http://127.0.0.1:8888/search?q=how+does+a+bill+become+law+in+the+Danish+parliament+Folketinget+process&format=json&language=all": {
   "body": "{\"results\": [{\"title\": \"The Parliament / The Danish Parliament\", \"url\": \"https://www.thedanishparliament.dk/en/democracy/the-parliament\", \"content\": \"The legislative process The Parliament and the Government hold the legislative power. The Government and the Members of Parliament can propose new laws, but only Parliament can pass the proposed laws (Bills). Each year, the Danish Parliament reads around 200 Bills. Laws regulate: how we live together in Denmark what we do together how the public (e.g., public schools and hospitals) must be ...\"}, {\"title\": \"How Laws Are Made in Denmark: The Legislative Process | Danify ...\", \"url\": \"https://danify.dk/en/blog/how-laws-are-made-in-denmark-the-legislative-process-explain-momkd6pp/\", \"content\": \"The Three Readings: How a Bill Becomes Law Once a bill is introduced, it must pass through three formal readings (behandlinger) in the Folketing before it can become law. This structured process ensures that legislation is carefully examined and debated. First Reading The first reading is primarily a general debate. Members of Parliament discuss the overall purpose and direction of the bill ...\"}, {\"title\": \"Frontpage / The Danish Parliament\", \"url\": \"https://www.thedanishparliament.dk/-/\", \"content\": \"Members of the Danish Parliament discuss policy in the Chamber. It is also in the Chamber that Bills are passed and become law. However, the Danish Parliament’s decisions are prepared by parliamentary committees. The Constitutional Act is the Danish constitution.\"}, {\"title\": \"Lovgivningsprocessen / Folketinget\", \"url\": \"https://www.ft.dk/da/folkestyret/folketinget/lovgivningsprocessen-i-folketinget\", \"content\": \"Folketinget har selv vedtaget en minimumsbehandlingstid for lovforslag på 40 dage. Det står i Folketingets forretningsorden. Denne frist skal sikre tid til en grundig behandling under arbejdet med lovforslagene, så lovene ikke er båret af en pludselig oppisket stemning.\"}, {\"title\": \"Hvordan vedtages en lov i Folketinget? / Folketinget\", \"url\": \"https://www.ft.dk/da/ofte-stillede-spoergsmaal/lov_hvordan-vedtages-en-lov-i-folketinget\", \"content\": \"Derudover skal det behandles i et af Folketingets faste udvalg. Alle lovforslag skal gennem en 1. behandling, en 2. behandling og en 3. behandling. Undervejs skal det også behandles minimum en gang i et af de faste fagudvalg. Ved 3. og sidste behandling vedtager eller forkaster Folketinget lovforslaget. Lovforslag vedtages med flertal.\"}, {\"title\": \"PDF The Danish Parliament and EU affairs - europarl.europa.eu\", \"url\": \"https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2025/772873/EPRS_BRI(2025)772873_EN.pdf\", \"content\": \"Both the government and Members of Parliament can introduce new legislation, but only the Parliament can pass the proposed laws. The legislative process is designed to provide time for debate and reflection. A bill cannot be finally adopted before three readings in the Folketing, and 40 days must have passed since its presentation.\"}, {\"title\": \"Legislative Flow - Danish Parliament API Documentation\", \"url\": \"https://brokk-sindre.github.io/ft-oda-documentation/data-model/parliamentary-process/legislative-flow/\", \"content\": \"Legislative Flow This document visualizes the complete Danish parliamentary legislative process using Mermaid diagrams, showing how cases (Sag) progress through the system from initial proposal to final decision. Overview ¶ The Danish Parliament (Folketinget) uses a complex multi-stage process for handling legislative cases.\"}, {\"title\": \"Folketing - Wikipedia\", \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folketing\", \"content\": \"Bills are predominantly brought ... have the Law Office of the Ministry of Justice at their disposal. Instead of putting forward a private bill, the opposition usually put forward a proposal for parliamentary decision, i.e., a short resolution that addresses the subject and directs the relevant minister to propose a bill concerning it. The 179 members of the folketing are directly elected to four-year terms, subject to calls for early elections. All Danish citizens 18 ...\"}]}"
