  "https://www.thelocal.dk/20240305/explained-how-a-new-law-gets-made-in-denmark": {
   "body": "<html><title>EXPLAINED: How a new law gets made in Denmark</title><body><p>EXPLAINED: How a new law gets made in Denmark</p>\n<p>Michael Barrett - michael.barrett@thelocal.com</p>\n<p>Updated: Sun 5 Jul 2026 07:21 CET</p>\n<p>Denmark's 'Folketingssalen' is where new laws are voted on, but what does it take for a new law to be made? Photo;: Mads Claus Rasmussen/Ritzau Scanpix</p>\n<p>Add The Local as a preferred source</p>\n<p>Arguably one of the keys to Denmark's success as a nation is the thorough, systematic way that government proposals get turned into laws.</p>\n<p>The process is highly formalised, with the Danish government's website having a section to the right of each lovforslag or proposed law showing where it is in the  lovgivningsproces,  or legislative process, the succession of stages each law goes through until it is passed in parliament.</p>\n<p>The first stage of any new law in Denmark is, of course, the idea.</p>\n<p>A proposal might be floated by a government minister in a newspaper, an opposition MP, a business leader, an organisation, at a press conference, in a speech, or in a party manifesto. It may have been debated back and forth for decades, but without any formal steps being taken.</p>\n<p>Until it moves on to the next stage it doesn't mean very much.</p>\n<p>Don't miss our journalists' daily news roundup from Denmark</p>\n<p>The first stage of the actual law-making process in Denmark is the lovforslag or beslutningsforslag , the two types of proposed law or change to be investigated and analysed.</p>\n<p>This is when an idea goes beyond talk and the process is in motion.</p>\n<p>The proposal summarises what proposal or idea </p>\n</body></html>"
  },
  "http://127.0.0.1:8888/search?q=role+of+the+Danish+government+in+Folketinget+law+making&format=json&language=all": {
   "body": "{\"results\": [{\"title\": \"Frontpage / The Danish Parliament\", \"url\": \"https://www.thedanishparliament.dk/-/\", \"content\": \"The Constitutional Act is the Danish constitution. It describes, among other things, the organization of the representative government, the citizens' rights and duties, and the tripartition of power.\"}, {\"title\": \"The Danish Government | A parliamentary democracy | denmark.dk\", \"url\": \"https://denmark.dk/society-and-business/government-and-politics\", \"content\": \"Danish democracy builds on a 175-year-old Constitution The framework for Danish democracy is the Danish Constitution of 1849, making it one of the oldest constitutions in the world. This Grundlov, or basic law, is a set of fundamental principles and rules for society that other laws must comply with, such as freedom of expression and freedom of assembly. Constitution Day is celebrated every ...\"}, {\"title\": \"The Parliament / The Danish Parliament\", \"url\": \"https://www.thedanishparliament.dk/en/democracy/the-parliament\", \"content\": \"The legislative process The Parliament and the Government hold the legislative power. The Government and the Members of Parliament can propose new laws, but only Parliament can pass the proposed laws (Bills). Each year, the Danish Parliament reads around 200 Bills. Laws regulate: how we live together in Denmark what we do together how the public (e.g., public schools and hospitals) must be ...\"}, {\"title\": \"Folketing - Wikipedia\", \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folketing\", \"content\": \"It passes all laws, approves the cabinet, and supervises the work of the government. It is also responsible for adopting the state's budgets and approving the state's accounts. As set out in the Constitution of Denmark, the Folketing shares power with the reigning monarch.\"}, {\"title\": \"The Danish Parliament (Folketinget) Explained for Expats 2026\", \"url\": \"https://denmarkexpat.com/the-danish-parliament-explained/\", \"content\": \"Jul 22, 2026 · Want to know how decisions in the Folketing will affect your job, taxes, benefits or stay in Denmark? This guide cuts through the formality and shows you what matters to you as an expat: who makes laws, how they get passed, and the quickest ways to follow or influence them.\"}, {\"title\": \"Politics of Denmark - Wikipedia\", \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politics_of_Denmark\", \"content\": \"The opposition rarely requests ... however, government policy is often discussed in the plenary assembly of Parliament. Since 1953, the year that marked the reform of the Danish constitution, parliament has been unicameral. With the implementation of the first democratic constitution in 1849, Denmark's legislature was constituted as a bicameral parliament, or Rigsdag, composed of Folketinget (a lower house ...\"}, {\"title\": \"Folketingets arbejde / Folketinget\", \"url\": \"https://www.ft.dk/da/folkestyret/folketinget/folketingets-arbejde\", \"content\": \"Folketinget er Danmarks parlament. Her vedtages al lovgivning i Danmark. Folketingets grundlæggende opgaver er beskrevet i grundloven. Folketinget og regeringen er de eneste, der kan fremsætte lovforslag, dvs. komme med forslag til nye love og lovændringer.\"}, {\"title\": \"Forside / Folketinget\", \"url\": \"https://www.ft.dk/?._.\", \"content\": \"Har du spørgsmål om Folketinget, lovgivningen eller Christiansborg, kan du kontakte Folketingets Oplysning og få hurtigt svar. Har du spørgsmål om arbejdet i EU eller dine rettigheder inden for EU, kan du kontakte Folketingets EU-Oplysning og få hurtigt svar. Find dokument på nummer og samling.\"}]}"
  },
